# Dedicated build context for Dockerfile.swoole.
# Docker uses this file automatically when building with `-f Dockerfile.swoole`.
#
# Difference from the root .dockerignore: composer.json, composer.lock and the
# JS/CSS assets stay IN the context (reproducible install plus a working UI),
# while Wasmer config, deployment descriptors and local data stay OUT.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.md
ChangeLog
Makefile
Vagrantfile
web.config
.dockerignore
*.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
custom-hooks
tests
docs
plugins/*
data/*

# Rebuilt inside the image from the unchanged lockfile.
vendor/

# Wasmer Edge bridge (live DB credentials, mail secrets), deployment
# descriptors and local environment files are never part of the image.
config.php
wasmer.toml
app.yaml
.env*

# Legacy container layers; only docker/swoole belongs in this image.
docker/etc
docker/usr
docker/var

# Stray local databases, never baked into the image.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
